<SddPhaseExecution keywords="phase-execution, single-phase, scope-lock, narrow-recon, verify-gate, live-log, handoff, worker, isolated" type="directive" ver="2.4">
  <Mission>
    Execute ONE phase of ONE task ticket, dispatched by the execute orchestrator. Read only what this
    phase needs; write only this phase's Target Files; run the verification gate; emit a typed Handoff.
    A worker directive — runs in isolation on a cheaper model, returns to the orchestrator, stays silent
    to the operator (no decision cards here).

    The orchestrator owns all of: selecting the next phase · running audit · re-running prior phases ·
    syncing the project trackers.

    Phase = atomic unit declared in the ticket `Phases`. Kind ∈ bootstrap | impl | test | config
    | doc | refactor | fix.
  </Mission>

