  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_PHASE_NOT_FOUND` | Phase ID from the orchestrator matches no block under `Phases` |
    | `H_PHASE_ALREADY_DONE` | Phase Status is `[x]` and no `fix` reason was passed |
    | `H_RECON_DIVERGENCE` | Recon shows Target Files inconsistent with the phase plan |
    | `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE` | A rule cited in the phase Rules list does not resolve |
    | `H_INPUT_HANDOFF_MISSING` | A phase Input cites a prior phase whose Handoff is absent in the current Round |
    | `H_OUT_OF_PHASE_WRITE` | A write is required outside Target Files or outside `AX_TICKET_WRITE_SCOPE` |
    | `H_THIRD_PARTY_API_UNVERIFIABLE` | `config` kind: network blocked AND local docs insufficient to verify a tool's current API |
    | `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL` | The verification gate fails after fix attempts (or tooling is missing) |
    | `H_BLOCKED` | Generic blocker per `AX_BLOCKER_ESCALATION` |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ContextExpectation>
    The orchestrator's dispatch prompt provides: the path to this directive; the ticket path; the target
    phase ID; a `fix` reason if this is a re-run; prior-phase Handoff payloads (current Round); and the
    **read-manifest** for this phase from `sdd-task` — the exact set to read (rule anchors, spec anchors,
    ticket sections, Target Files) plus a "do not read" boundary and a rough line budget.

    Per `AX_READ_PER_MANIFEST`: read EXACTLY the manifest, nothing beyond it. Pull each cited block by
    anchor (`sdd-extract <file> <ANCHOR>`), not whole files. Something needed but absent from the
    manifest → emit a `discovery` line and surface it; keep the read within the manifest.
  </ContextExpectation>

  <PhaseProcedure>
    <Step id="STEP_1_PARSE_PHASE_INPUT">
      <Goal>Resolve the phase, validate prerequisites, record the reason for this run.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read Meta + Phases Overview + the target phase block. Missing block → `H_PHASE_NOT_FOUND`; Status
        `[x]` without a `fix` reason → `H_PHASE_ALREADY_DONE`. For each Input, locate the prior phase's
        `**Handoff →**` line in the current Round (missing → `H_INPUT_HANDOFF_MISSING`). Append the phase
        header to the current Round: `#### <PhaseID>` (or `… — re-run: <reason>` for `fix`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_NARROW_RECON">
      <Goal>Verify ground truth before writing — log only on divergence.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per `AX_NARROW_RECON`: log a recon line ONLY on divergence; when state matches the plan, stay
        silent. On divergence emit a `discovery` line; if it breaks the phase contract → `H_RECON_DIVERGENCE`, else proceed.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_LOAD_RULES">
      <Goal>Internalize the rules governing this phase. No log line.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Read the rule anchors in the manifest (`AX_RULES_LOAD_FROM_PHASE_BLOCK` + `AX_READ_PER_MANIFEST`) —
        the bounded set already filtered by phase kind + Target Files, by anchor not whole file. A cited
        anchor that fails to resolve → `H_MISSING_RULE_FILE`. Skip the `rules` log line — the manifest declares them.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3B_TOOL_API">
      <Goal>`config` kind only: verify the CURRENT API of every third-party tool this phase configures (`AX_THIRD_PARTY_TOOL_CURRENT_API`). Any other kind skips this step.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Per tool, BEFORE writing any config:
        1. Installed version: read `<modules-dir>/<pkg>/package.json` field `version`.
        2. Local CHANGELOG (recent major + previous): look for `BREAKING`, `deprecated`, `removed`, `migration`.
        3. Local README: current-version config syntax.
        4. Local docs minimal → WebFetch homepage from `package.json#homepage` / `repository.url`.
        5. Network blocked AND local docs insufficient → `H_THIRD_PARTY_API_UNVERIFIABLE` — halt rather
           than guess or apply a training-default silently.
        Then log: `<ts> verified <tool>@<version> <one-line summary>` — audit requires this entry per
        config artifact.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_EXECUTE">
      <Goal>Produce the artifacts the phase Objective demands, within Target Files.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Apply rules continuously; respect `AX_PHASE_SCOPE_LOCK`, `AX_FILE_HEADER_APPEND_ONLY`,
        `AX_INTRODUCED_DISCIPLINE`. `test` kind honors `AX_BDD_NAME_DISCIPLINE`; `config` kind applies
        the current-version API verified at STEP_3B (`AX_THIRD_PARTY_TOOL_CURRENT_API`). Append event
        lines per `AX_LIVE_LOG`; a
        spec gap goes to an `insight` line and leaves the spec untouched (`AX_SPEC_NEVER_EDITED`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_VERIFY">
      <Goal>Run the verification gate, then the ticket §5 commands. Log only final results.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Run `sdd-verify --profile <by kind>` (commands stay within `AX_PERMITTED_BASH_COMMANDS`; the deterministic gate, exact `npm run` scripts, mutating
        first, run-all, brief on pass, details on fail). Profile by phase kind: `impl` / `refactor` /
        `config` / `doc` / `bootstrap` → `code` (format · lint · typecheck — a code phase skips tests);
        `test` → `test` (format · typecheck · test:coverage); a `fix` phase takes the profile of
        the kind it repairs. The full set runs once at the end (orchestrator close, not here). For
        `impl` / `refactor` / `test` phases also run `gennady lint --spec=<this module's spec> <Target Files>`
        — closed-world inventory sync (`ERR_CLI_LINT_INVENTORY_UNDECLARED`) + cast safety
        (`ERR_CLI_LINT_UNSAFE_CAST`). An exported entity not in the inventory is drift
        (`AX_CLOSED_WORLD_INVENTORY`): remove it, or — if genuinely needed — log an `intro <name> ← <reason>`
        line (`AX_INTRODUCED_DISCIPLINE`; the worker leaves the spec to audit, `AX_SPEC_NEVER_EDITED` — the intro
        line flags it for inventory backflow at audit). MUST resolve every out-of-inventory export this way. A cast → remove (proper type / guard) or a documented `@ts-expect-error` (`AX_NO_SILENT_ESCAPE_HATCH` — never a silent suppression).
        Then run each ticket §5 command **verbatim** (the Canonical Gate per `AX_VERIFICATION_BEFORE_HANDOFF`),
        exactly as written. **Error ownership:** this session MUST fix every failure the gate surfaces —
        edited or not, in scope or not, pre-existing or not. Treat each as an error still to fix. Fix all,
        re-run, then log one `ver <exact-cmd> → pass exit=<N>` per command. A fix that
        breaks the phase contract → `H_BLOCKED` (surfaced as PAUSED awaiting the operator, not as failure —
        `AX_HALT_VS_FAIL_DISTINCTION`; the `🛑 BLOCKED` log line opens the resolution trail the
        orchestrator checks, `AX_BLOCKER_RESOLUTION_TRAIL`); missing tooling → `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL`. A `ver` line MUST
        reflect a command actually run verbatim; logging one otherwise is fabricated verification (audit BLOCKER).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_EMIT_HANDOFF">
      <Goal>Close the phase block with a typed Handoff and DONE.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Append `<ts> DONE`; append the `**Handoff →**` line per `HANDOFF_FORMAT` (typed payload,
        `AX_HANDOFF_TYPED`); flip this phase's Status
        in Phases Overview `[ ]` → `[x]`; return the structured summary per `RETURN_SUMMARY_FORMAT` to the
        orchestrator.
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </PhaseProcedure>

